## 2026-11-08 — SerpApi and Kroger API review

- SerpApi's current pricing page lists 250 searches/month at $0 and $25/month for 1,000 searches. Its Google Shopping API returns parsed Shopping results and supports a location parameter; it is a third-party scraper, not a Google Shopping API. Its terms say search data accuracy is not guaranteed and the U.S. Legal Shield excludes Free, Starter, and Developer plans, while the pricing page appears to list the Shield in the Free row; treat that conflict as unresolved and do not rely on free-plan coverage.
- Kroger's official public workspace requires account and app registration for OAuth credentials. Its product search can use a store location ID for location-specific products/prices. I found no official public price schedule. The official Acceptable Use policy appears to restrict comparing Kroger prices with other retailers, so it does not fit the current cross-store comparison goal; partner APIs require an agreement.
- No provider switch was made. Open Prices remains selected for the project because its public read data has an explicit ODbL reuse path; its sparse and dated observations remain a known limitation. No SerpApi request was made because no account key is configured.

