## 2026-11-08 — Raw beef / stew-cut Open Prices verification

- Repeated read-only API checks around Hayward (37.6688, -122.0808) at 5, 25, and 50 miles. These use explicit `type` and category/product filters; no empty product-ID query was sent.
- Open Prices does contain beef-related prices. Its priced-product catalog returned 513 product entries matching `beef` globally. This is a broad global count and includes many prepared foods, jerky, ground beef, and other items; it does not mean 513 raw beef cuts or local stock.
- Within 25 and 50 miles, the `type=CATEGORY&category_tag=en:beef-steaks` lookup found one observation: Trader Joe's, Mountain View, $46.28 USD/kg, dated 2025-10-11. The same lookup returned zero at 5 miles. It is tagged as beef steaks, so it is not a verified stew-cut price.
- Checked likely category tags `en:beef-steaks`, `en:beef-roasts`, `en:beef-cuts`, `en:stew-meats`, and `en:beef-stew-meat`: only the steak tag had a local observation (one at 25 miles and the same one at 50 miles); all tags returned zero at 5 miles.
- The 50-mile category-price pages contained seven meat-related records when filtered by category tag. Beef appeared only as the single `en:beef-steaks` record; the others were chicken. No raw stew-meat category record appeared in that radius/page scan.
- Product-linked API lookups for `product__categories_tags__contains=en:beef` returned no records at 5 miles; the 25-mile results were mostly ground beef and processed beef items. For the broader `en:beef-and-its-products` filter, 71 rows were returned at 25 and 50 miles, but the cut-like candidates were ground products, patties, or packaged steak strips; none is a confirmed raw stew cut. Results did not establish a Hayward-city beef price.
- The product catalog's global `brisket` search returned four priced products (beef patties, smoked brisket ravioli, brisket pho, and brisket-flavored chips), not raw brisket cuts. Exact `stew meat` and `beef cubes` searches returned zero priced catalog matches.
- Diagnosis: there is an implementation gap and a source-coverage gap. The Worker only searches barcode-linked products, so it omits `CATEGORY` observations; adding category lookup can help for appropriate tags. However, the verified local category observation is for steaks, not stew cuts, so do not silently display it as stew beef. Open Prices' local community data currently does not provide a confirmed raw stew-cut price in these checks.
- Proposed follow-up: adjust ingredient normalization so “beef stew” yields an explicit raw-cut intent (e.g., raw chuck/stewing beef; never ground beef or canned stew); search product and category records separately; enforce cut/type exclusions; use the closest radius with accurate distance ordering; and return “No verified matching price record” when no cut match exists. Keep expanding radius and broader beef-category fallback opt-in/clearly labeled. No Worker/UI code changed during this verification.

