## 2026-11-08 — Deployment, security, stop options, and AI Search research

- User asked what is deployed, how the Worker and GitHub Pages interact, whether it is secure, how to stop it, and whether a 50-mile Open Prices snapshot plus Cloudflare AI Search could improve ingredient matching. No new deployment, storage, AI Search instance, or stop action was requested or performed.
- Verified the public GitHub Pages P3 URL still serves the older `Project 3` placeholder and `main` is at `1a31a87`; the new Basket Buddy frontend remains on `ken` (`9d0538c`) pending the user's manual pull request/merge. The production Worker exists at `https://basket-buddy-api.xoakuma.workers.dev` and is configured in the unpublished frontend.
- Reviewed Worker source: it uses HTTPS, a Cloudflare Workers AI binding, origin checking and request bounds, but no authentication or application-level rate limiting. CORS is not access control: requests with no `Origin` are allowed, and non-browser clients can spoof headers. Do not claim the Worker is protected from public abuse or that meal text never reaches an external service. The app sends meal requests to Workers AI and ingredient names to Open Prices; there is no app persistence, though Cloudflare may retain operational metadata under its policy.
- `workers.dev` can be disabled via Cloudflare Workers & Pages > worker > Settings > Domains & Routes; preview/version URLs are separate and future Wrangler deploys can re-enable the route. Deleting the Worker is a separate action. GitHub Pages unpublish affects the entire repository's site, not only P3. Stopping local Wrangler does not stop the deployed Worker.
- Open Prices 50-mile unfiltered prices query returned 42,342 observations on this date; these are not unique products, guaranteed local inventory, or live prices. Open Prices publishes separate daily gzipped JSONL exports (prices/products/locations/proofs); alternatively page through the API's 50-mile filter. Cloudflare AI Search supports `.json` and 10 MiB plain-text files, but the documented type list does not list `.jsonl.gz`; transform and/or split before testing. Build a product/candidate index with source IDs and store price data separately, use semantic+keyword retrieval and deterministic checks/price handling, and refresh regularly. Do not expect it to fix absent coverage, outdated observations, or guarantee food matches.
- Cloudflare's AI Search limits/pricing page lists 5M ingestion tokens, 10 GB-month and 1,000 semantic plus 1,000 full-text queries per month included; generation and query rewriting may be billed separately. The pricing page says billing begins 2026-12-01, while its release note says 2026-11-01. Verify the user's account and actual dashboard billing before enabling. A hypothetical ten semantic searches per basket would use 1,000 semantic queries for 100 baskets; batching/caching can change that. These monthly allocations differ from Workers AI's daily Neuron allowance.
- Sources: https://openfoodfacts.github.io/open-prices/guides/data/ ; https://developers.cloudflare.com/ai-search/configuration/data-source/ ; https://developers.cloudflare.com/ai-search/platform/limits-pricing/ ; https://developers.cloudflare.com/ai-search/platform/release-note/ ; https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/platform/data-usage/ ; https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/routing/workers-dev/ .

## 2026-11-08 — Public access protection options and data storage

- User asked to secure the Worker against unauthorized use and asked whether GitHub is a good place for the 50-mile Open Prices snapshot/index. They clarified that sign-in is undesirable. A follow-up choice between Turnstile plus rate limits, rate limits alone, or disabling the public Worker is pending; do not claim the live Worker is secured or deploy a choice-specific change before that choice.
- Cloudflare Turnstile has a free plan, supports pages hosted elsewhere, and requires server-side Siteverify validation with a Cloudflare-stored secret; it can reduce automated abuse but does not identify authorized users. Workers rate-limit bindings are approximate and per Cloudflare location, not strict worldwide spending limits; Cloudflare warns that rate-limiting by IP can group legitimate users behind shared networks.
- Read-only HEAD requests showed the full global compressed Open Prices prices export at 22,774,156 bytes and products export at 20,322,550 bytes on this date. These are not the 50-mile subset or uncompressed sizes. The 50-mile price API count remained 42,342 observations. GitHub can host a small demo file but its docs recommend generated data outside Git; repeated snapshots inflate repository history and an individual Git object is limited to 100 MB.
- Suggested future prototype: a small 50-mile, source-attributed set indexed in AI Search's built-in storage (or R2), structured product IDs and prices separately, semantic+keyword retrieval for candidate names, and source-backed exact price/date/store/unit handling in Worker code. Use a small sample and compare results before full ingestion or spending; maintain a refresh method. No data export or Cloudflare storage/index was created.
- References: https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/get-started/ ; https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/plans/ ; https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/bindings/rate-limit/ ; https://developers.cloudflare.com/ai-search/configuration/data-source/built-in-storage/ ; https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/creating-and-managing-repositories/repository-limits .

